<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sumbawa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sumbawa is an island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>'s Lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a> chain, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombok">Lombok</a> and Flores. It was divided among several small kingdoms and sultanates, including Sumbawa, Bima and Dompu, which had close ties with Makassar. The eruption of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-tambora">Mount Tambora</a> in 1815, the largest in recorded history, destroyed the kingdoms of Tambora and Pekat on the island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sumbawa.jpg" alt="Sumbawa" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tofifoto · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pacoa_Jara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
